00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.150 align:start position:0%
at a cemetery northeast of gaza city two  hamas policemen  killed in tuesday night's attacks were  brought for burial  in all three policemen were killed in  two separate blasts  hamas's gaza police chief was here to  mourn his men  and promise a strong reaction  we have made arrests and we are  investigating people to ensure we get to  anyone who could be responsible for the  attacks  but things are under control and the  security status is good  daily life is back to normal gaza's  interior ministry says two suicide  bombers carried out the coordinated  attacks  on two checkpoints two policemen were  killed and a bystander injured in the  first explosion  the third policeman died in the second  blast minutes later  by day police were back on duty where  their colleagues had died  reinforcements stationed on streets  throughout the city hamas  announcing a general alert for all the  instability and violence the people of  gaza have had to get used to in recent  years  these attacks have still sent a ripple  of shock around the territory  targeting the very institution that is  supposed to provide internal security  and right here in the heart of gaza city  the attacks are widely believed here to  be the work of salafi groups  with links to isil in 2016 hamas agreed  to help  egypt in its fight against isil fighters  in the sinai peninsula  restricting their movement across the  egypt gaza border  i believe that as we see further  security coordination and cooperation  between hamas security services and  egyptian security approaches it seems to  me that we see  further tension between hamas and isil  further bloodshed between hamas and isil  as we saw saw it last night and i don't  think this is going to be the last  incident  this month has already seen increased  instability with rockets fired into  israel  attempts by armed men to breach the  border fence israeli airstrikes and  artillery fire  targeting gaza now a source of internal  instability has been made fatally clear  hamas is insisting it will maintain  security  and punish those behind the attacks  harry fawcett  al jazeera gaza
 

